title: Monstrous Hybrid
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

Pick up a juice carton, a [[Tetra Pak]]. It is paperboard, plastic, and aluminum foil, pressed into one sheet.

The paper could rot. The foil could be melted down and used again. Stuck together, neither can happen on its own.

[[Cradle to Cradle]] calls this a monstrous hybrid: materials joined so they can't simply be separated. The worst kind joins a [[Biological Nutrient]] to a [[Technical Nutrient]], so that neither cycle gets its material back.

Two cases:

* [[Tetra Pak]]: the paper half gets a second life, and the hybrid half stays a hybrid
* [[Juice Pouch]]: the harder case, with no paper in it at all

The [[Catifa Carta]] is built to avoid it. The shell and the frame come apart. The [[Oka Chair]] is also nearly all biological materials, but they disassemble with physical fasteners… [[Peel Chair]] avoids it too by being ALL hemp derived plastic. The [[Think Chair]] from [[Steelcase]] also comes fully apart to allow for separation of plastic parts and metal parts, etc.

See [[PolyAl]], [[Downcycling]], [[Recyclable, but really?]]
